message: "If you use or discuss this research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Adaptive Invariant Computation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Timms"
    given-names: "Martin"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-30"
abstract: >-
  Adaptive Invariant Computation (AIC) is a research programme investigating
  whether task-relevant invariants can provide a principled boundary for
  reducing computational representations while preserving useful structure.
  The work develops from ideas explored in Bindu Recursive Compression Theory
  (BRCT), invariant-space learning, and inversion/reversion as a means of
  testing information preservation.
repository-code: "https://github.com/Electro-resonance/Adaptive-Invariant-Computation"
keywords:
  - adaptive invariant computation
  - invariant learning
  - recursive compression
  - representation learning
  - efficient AI
  - inversion
  - reversion
  - BRCT
